  (@custom "contractspecv0" (after data) "\00\00\00\00\00\00\00!The compiled-in verification key.\00\00\00\00\00\00\02vk\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\1d`ZkAdapterInterface::verify`: `Ok(())` iff `evidence` proves, for\0aexactly `statement`, knowledge of the credential enrolled under\0a`binding`, against a root `binding.pool` has had for\0a`evidence.tree_id`. Writes nothing; nullifier bookkeeping and evidence\0afreshness are the controller's.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06verify\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09statement\00\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11RecoveryStatement\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07binding\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\09ZkBinding\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08evidence\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aZkEvidence\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eZkAdapterError\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00mThe adapter's semantics version ([`VERSION`](crate::VERSION)). A new\0aversion is a new wasm and a new address.\00\00\00\00\00\00\07version\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00v`sha256` of the compiled-in verification key: the circuit identity an\0aaccount's configuration names in its ZK binding.\00\00\00\00\00\0acircuit_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\d0`ZkAdapterInterface::tree_depth`: the Merkle depth the compiled-in\0acircuit proves ([`CIRCUIT_DEPTH`](crate::CIRCUIT_DEPTH)). The\0acontroller checks it against the pool's `depth()` when a ZK factor is\0aenrolled.\00\00\00\0atree_depth\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\f8`ProofVerifierInterface::verify_proof`: the raw verifier, for callers\0athat assemble public inputs themselves. `ProofParseError` means the\0aproof is not a zero-knowledge proof's length. Same ABI and error codes\0aas Nido's old `nido-recovery-verifier`.\00\00\00\0cverify_proof\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dpublic_inputs\00\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproof_bytes\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\12ProofVerifierError\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00,What a completion hands back to the account.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aCompletion\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\1bThe attempt that completed.\00\00\00\00\0aattempt_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\02\10The credentials that occupied the replaced signer slots **in the\0aattempt's source document**, as derived at T1: the applied document\0afor lost-key, the baseline for compromise. The account fingerprints\0athem over canonical keys and revokes them together with every\0acredential the completion removed from its current document. Without\0athese, a baseline credential replaced by a compromise recovery, and\0aalready absent from the current document, would stay unrevoked and\0acould be restored by a later recovery from the same baseline.\00\00\00\08replaced\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00XWhat `rcv_sync` did, so the account knows which of its own effects to\0aapply (spec \c2\a710).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bSyncOutcome\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1fNothing about recovery changed.\00\00\00\00\09Unchanged\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\000A configuration was enrolled at this controller.\00\00\00\08Enrolled\00\00\00\00\00\00\00(The enrolled configuration was replaced.\00\00\00\0cReconfigured\00\00\00\00\00\00\00uThe configuration was removed from this controller (recovery\0aremoved, or the account switched to another controller).\00\00\00\00\00\00\07Removed\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\01sThe authorized attempt completed in this invocation. The account\0ainserts the new leaf if the enrollment id changed, records the\0aenrollment id, revokes [`Completion::replaced`] together with every\0acredential the completion removed from its current document (spec \c2\a78;\0a`credential::revocations` computes the union), clears\0aits pending upgrade, and clears its freeze mirror.\00\00\00\00\09Completed\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aCompletion\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00HWhich phase of an account upgrade `rcv_upgrade` is checking (spec \c2\a712).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bUpgradeStep\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\95`schedule_upgrade`: refuse during an authorized window; under\0a`Protected`, require recorded approvals of this subject valid through\0athe given ledger.\00\00\00\00\00\00\08Schedule\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eUpgradeSubject\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\85`execute_upgrade` of a request recorded at this epoch: refuse during\0aan authorized window or if the epoch moved, then bump the epoch.\00\00\00\00\00\00\07Execute\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\a1Everything a recovery controller can refuse. Codes are sequential from 1\0ain declaration order and are wire format: append new variants at the\0aend, never reorder.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dRecoveryError\00\00\00\00\00\00\1f\00\00\00ANo configuration is enrolled for this account at this controller.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bNotEnrolled\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\80An attempt is authorized and live: begin, policy changes, and upgrades are refused until it completes, is cancelled, or expires.\00\00\00\11AttemptAuthorized\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00/No attempt with this id exists for the account.\00\00\00\00\0dNoSuchAttempt\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00cThe attempt is terminal, expired, from an older epoch, or invalidated by a sibling's authorization.\00\00\00\00\0eAttemptNotLive\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00@Initiation evidence for an attempt that is no longer collecting.\00\00\00\14AttemptNotCollecting\00\00\00\05\00\00\00%Completion before `executable_after`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\10NotExecutableYet\00\00\00\06\00\00\00fThe completion context, or the compiled document hash, does not match the authorized attempt's target.\00\00\00\00\00\0bWrongTarget\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00(The address is not an enrolled guardian.\00\00\00\0cNotAGuardian\00\00\00\08\00\00\00;This guardian or factor already counted for this statement.\00\00\00\00\0eAlreadyCounted\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00)The enrolled mode has no guardian factor.\00\00\00\00\00\00\12ModeHasNoGuardians\00\00\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00#The enrolled mode has no ZK factor.\00\00\00\00\0bModeHasNoZk\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00>The adapter refused the proof (its `ZkAdapterError` says why).\00\00\00\00\00\12ZkEvidenceRejected\00\00\00\00\00\0c\00\00\00\1fThe proof's nullifier is spent.\00\00\00\00\0eNullifierSpent\00\00\00\00\00\0d\00\00\00>The statement's freshness bound has passed or reaches too far.\00\00\00\00\00\0fEvidenceExpired\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00GThe statement cannot be encoded (a non-contract account or controller).\00\00\00\00\10InvalidStatement\00\00\00\0f\00\00\00]Recorded approvals do not satisfy the enrolled condition for this reconfiguration or upgrade.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fConditionNotMet\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00'The account's `max-cancels` is used up.\00\00\00\00\11MaxCancelsReached\00\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\002Owner cancellation is only available under `Loss`.\00\00\00\00\00\12OwnerCancelRefused\00\00\00\00\00\12\00\00\00BThe replacement set breaks a \c2\a77.3 rule, or derivation refused it.\00\00\00\00\00\13InvalidReplacements\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00:The target or a replacement contains a revoked credential.\00\00\00\00\00\11CredentialRevoked\00\00\00\00\00\00\14\00\00\00\b2The ZK enrollment id was enrolled for this account before (the controller checks the account's `is_enrolled_id` at T1; the pure `derive_target` cannot see the account's history).\00\00\00\00\00\12EnrollmentIdReused\00\00\00\00\00\15\00\00\00.Compromise recovery with no baseline enrolled.\00\00\00\00\00\0aNoBaseline\00\00\00\00\00\16\00\00\00@Compromise recovery before the baseline's content was published.\00\00\00\14BaselineNotPublished\00\00\00\17\00\00\00>The published document does not hash to the enrolled baseline.\00\00\00\00\00\10BaselineMismatch\00\00\00\18\00\00\00SThe adapter's circuit id or tree depth does not match the enrolled factor and pool.\00\00\00\00\10ZkWiringMismatch\00\00\00\19\00\00\002The ZK factor changed without a new enrollment id.\00\00\00\00\00\16ZkFactorChangedInPlace\00\00\00\00\00\1a\00\00\00uThe configuration is malformed (for example, the account is one of its own guardians, or the quorum is out of range).\00\00\00\00\00\00\14InvalidConfiguration\00\00\00\1b\00\00\001An upgrade request recorded under an older epoch.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cStaleUpgrade\00\00\00\1c\00\00\00/A ledger-sequence computation overflowed `u32`.\00\00\00\00\0eLedgerOverflow\00\00\00\00\00\1d\00\00\00=The policy was attached to a context rule of the wrong shape.\00\00\00\00\00\00\14MalformedContextRule\00\00\00\1e\00\00\00yA credential the replacement set replaces still appears in the target (a swap or a no-op replacement, spec \c2\a77.3 rule 8).\00\00\00\00\00\00\1aReplacedCredentialRetained\00\00\00\00\00\1f\00\00\00\02\00\00\00NA signer credential, shaped like OZ `stellar_accounts::smart_account::Signer`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\01\00\00\00l`Signer::Delegated(address)`: a `G...` or `C...` address that\0aauthenticates through CAP-0071 delegated auth.\00\00\00\09Delegated\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00H`Signer::External(verifier, key)`: a key checked by a verifier\0acontract.\00\00\00\08External\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00lOne designated signer slot and the credential that replaces whatever\0athat slot holds in the source document.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bReplacement\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\008The credential the target document gives that signer id.\00\00\00\0acredential\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aCredential\00\00\00\00\00CA document signer id listed in the enrolled `recovery.replaceable`.\00\00\00\00\09signer_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\01UA ZK enrollment a recovery completion installs.\0a\0aThe commitment is bound here, not only the id: completion runs under the\0azero-signer recovery rule, so nothing signs its arguments, and a\0acommitment supplied only at completion could be swapped by whoever\0asubmits the completing transaction first \e2\80\94 handing them the account's\0anext ZK factor.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cZkEnrollment\00\00\00\02\00\00\01\19The new leaf's inner commitment, `Poseidon2(DOM_LEAF, secret)`.\0aDerivation writes `id` and `commitment` into the target document's\0arecovery section, so the target hash binds them, and the completing\0a`apply_doc` inserts the leaf from the compiled target, never from a\0acall argument.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acommitment\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00MThe new enrollment id. Must never have been enrolled for this\0aaccount before.\00\00\00\00\00\00\02id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00oEverything a `LostKey`/`Compromise` attempt changes about the source\0adocument. See `docs/recovery/spec.md` \c2\a77.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eReplacementSet\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00uSigner replacements in strictly ascending `signer_id` byte order\0a(sorted, no duplicates) \e2\80\94 the one canonical order.\00\00\00\00\00\00\07signers\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bReplacement\00\00\00\01%The fresh ZK enrollment the completion installs, required exactly\0awhen the enrolled mode has a ZK factor (a ZK-evidenced completion\0aconsumes the enrolled credential, so it must install a fresh one).\0aEmpty or one entry \e2\80\94 a `Vec` because `#[contracttype]` cannot derive\0a`Option<CustomStruct>`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dzk_enrollment\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cZkEnrollment\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\8eWhich enrolled ZK factor a statement is checked against. The controller\0abuilds this from its stored configuration \e2\80\94 never from caller input.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09ZkBinding\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00uThe circuit identity the enrolling document named. The adapter\0arefuses any binding whose `circuit_id` is not its own.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acircuit_id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\c8The enrolled credential's id, bound into its leaf and its nullifier.\0aA leaf enrolled under any other id \e2\80\94 including the account's own\0aearlier enrollments \e2\80\94 cannot satisfy a proof for this binding.\00\00\00\0denrollment_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00EThe enrolled membership pool. Roots are accepted only from this pool.\00\00\00\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\1aOne ZK proof as submitted.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aZkEvidence\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00?The credential's nullifier (the circuit's second public input).\00\00\00\00\09nullifier\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\15The serialized proof.\00\00\00\00\00\00\05proof\00\00\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00`The root the proof was generated against; must be acceptable to the\0aenrolled pool for `tree_id`.\00\00\00\04root\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00,The pool tree the proof's Merkle path is in.\00\00\00\07tree_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\85Everything [`ZkAdapterInterface::verify`] can refuse. Each is a refusal\0aof this evidence only; none is a statement about the account.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eZkAdapterError\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\009The binding names a circuit this adapter does not verify.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fCircuitMismatch\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00XThe statement cannot be projected (its account or controller is not a contract address).\00\00\00\10InvalidStatement\00\00\00\02\00\00\007The root or nullifier is not a canonical field element.\00\00\00\00\11NonCanonicalField\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\004The enrolled pool does not accept `(tree_id, root)`.\00\00\00\0bUnknownRoot\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00&The enrolled pool could not be called.\00\00\00\00\00\0fPoolUnavailable\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\007The proof is not the length/shape the circuit produces.\00\00\00\00\0eMalformedProof\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00 The verifier rejected the proof.\00\00\00\0dProofRejected\00\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00@The verifier could not be called or failed to parse its own key.\00\00\00\13VerifierUnavailable\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\a8A backend verifier's refusals. Same names, order, and codes (1, 2, 3)\0aas Nido's constructorless `nido-recovery-verifier`, so either can sit\0abehind an adapter unchanged.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\12ProofVerifierError\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00)The verification key could not be parsed.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cVkParseError\00\00\00\01\00\00\00EThe proof could not be parsed (for example, it has the wrong length).\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fProofParseError\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\004The proof does not verify against the public inputs.\00\00\00\12VerificationFailed\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\02\00\00\00wWho may change the recovery configuration, and whether an authorized\0aattempt freezes ordinary activity (spec \c2\a72, \c2\a79).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fRecoveryProfile\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00wOwner authorization alone reconfigures; activity continues while an\0aattempt is authorized; the owner can always cancel.\00\00\00\00\04Loss\00\00\00\00\00\00\00iReconfiguration and upgrades also need the enrolled condition; an\0aauthorized attempt freezes the account.\00\00\00\00\00\00\09Protected\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\22The ZK factor (spec \c2\a73.1, \c2\a73.4).\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\05\00\00\004The constructorless ZK adapter the controller calls.\00\00\00\07adapter\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00T`sha256` of the adapter's verification key; must equal the adapter's\0a`circuit_id()`.\00\00\00\0acircuit_id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00rThe current credential's inner commitment, `Poseidon2(DOM_LEAF,\0asecret)`, from which the account inserts the leaf.\00\00\00\00\00\0acommitment\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00?The current credential's id, bound into its leaf and nullifier.\00\00\00\00\0denrollment_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00,The membership pool roots are accepted from.\00\00\00\04pool\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\14The guardian factor.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00@Guardian addresses (`G...` or `C...`), never the account itself.\00\00\00\09guardians\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00!`1 <= quorum <= guardians.len()`.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06quorum\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\02\00\00\00 Which factors a statement needs.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14CompiledRecoveryMode\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\16A quorum of guardians.\00\00\00\00\00\0cGuardianOnly\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0dOne ZK proof.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06ZkOnly\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\01\00\00\00'A quorum of guardians and one ZK proof.\00\00\00\00\08Combined\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\13CompiledGuardianSet\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10CompiledZkFactor\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\1dA compiled `recovery` member.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\16CompiledRecoveryConfig\00\00\00\00\00\09\00\00\00TThe enrolled baseline's canonical document hash, if compromise\0arecovery is enrolled.\00\00\00\08baseline\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\d4[`config_hash`] of the canonical JSON of the recovery member, computed\0aby the doc compiler (spec \c2\a73.2). Configuration\0aidentity: two compiled configurations with the same `config_hash` are\0athe same configuration.\00\00\00\0bconfig_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00 The adopted controller instance.\00\00\00\0acontroller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00>Ledgers from an attempt's authorization until it can complete.\00\00\00\00\00\0ddelay_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00gThe evidence window of a collecting attempt and the completion\0awindow of an authorized one, in ledgers.\00\00\00\00\0eexpiry_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00DLifetime cap on evidence-based cancellations of authorized attempts.\00\00\00\0bmax_cancels\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\22The factors evidence must satisfy.\00\00\00\00\00\04mode\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\14CompiledRecoveryMode\00\00\00XWho may change the configuration, and whether an authorized attempt\0afreezes the account.\00\00\00\07profile\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fRecoveryProfile\00\00\00\00{Signer ids (not credential fingerprints) a recovery may replace, so\0arotating a key does not change the configuration (#92).\00\00\00\00\0breplaceable\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\01\00\00\02aOne pending account upgrade (spec \c2\a712).\0a\0aStaleness is judged against the account's own **recovery generation**, a\0a`u64` the account keeps in its own storage. It starts at 0 and is never\0areset. It advances on every `rcv_sync` outcome other than `Unchanged`\0a(`controller::SyncOutcome::bumps_generation`) and on every executed\0aupgrade.\0a\0aThe controller's epoch cannot play this role. It belongs to one\0acontroller and does not exist while the account is unenrolled, so a\0arequest scheduled unenrolled would survive enrolling recovery and\0aremoving it again: the final state has no controller, just as at\0ascheduling.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eUpgradeRequest\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\95The adopted controller's epoch when scheduled, if a controller was\0aadopted. Passed back as `UpgradeStep::Execute` so the controller can\0acheck it too.\00\00\00\00\00\00\10controller_epoch\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\002The first ledger at which the request may execute.\00\00\00\00\00\0dexecutable_at\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00AThe account's recovery generation when the request was scheduled.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0ageneration\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\1aPer-account, never reused.\00\00\00\00\00\0arequest_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00$The exact Wasm the account will run.\00\00\00\09wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\02\00\00\00EWhat a `Reconfigure` statement changes the enrolled configuration to.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cConfigChange\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00!Remove recovery from the account.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06Remove\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\8bReplace the configuration with the one whose\0a[`ConfigBinding::config_hash`] is this value (which may name a\0adifferent controller instance).\00\00\00\00\03Set\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00$The subject of a `Cancel` statement.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dCancelSubject\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\1cThe attempt being cancelled.\00\00\00\0aattempt_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00tThat attempt's own initiation statement digest, so cancellation\0aevidence names exactly one proposal, not just an id.\00\00\00\11attempt_statement\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00<The enrolled configuration a statement is evaluated against.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dConfigBinding\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\01e`sha256(\22perch/recovery/config\22 || canonical JSON of the enrolled\0adocument's recovery member)`, as [`crate::config::config_hash`]\0acomputes it (`docs/recovery/spec.md` \c2\a73.2). Binds the whole\0aconfiguration: profile, mode, guardians, quorum, ZK adapter, circuit\0aid, pool, enrollment id and commitment, controller, baseline,\0areplaceable signer ids, and timing.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bconfig_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\e4The controller's per-account configuration epoch. It increments on\0aevery enrollment, reconfiguration, removal, completed recovery, and\0aexecuted account upgrade, so evidence produced under one epoch is\0adead under every later one.\00\00\00\05epoch\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\003The subject of a `LostKey` or `Compromise` attempt.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eAttemptSubject\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00>The controller-assigned, per-account, never-reused attempt id.\00\00\00\00\00\0aattempt_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00I[`crate::credential::ReplacementSet::hash`] of the declared\0areplacements.\00\00\00\00\00\00\11replacements_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\a3`LostKey`: the canonical hash of the account's applied document when\0athe attempt began (the agreed snapshot). `Compromise`: the enrolled\0abaseline's canonical hash.\00\00\00\00\0fsource_doc_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00|The canonical hash of the target document, derived on-chain from\0athe source and the replacement set \e2\80\94 never caller-chosen.\00\00\00\0ftarget_doc_hash\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\03\00\00\01JThe action domain a statement authorizes. Evidence for one action never\0asatisfies another: the action code is the encoding's 26th byte and selects\0athe subject layout, so two statements that differ only in action have\0adifferent digests (and different encoded lengths for most pairs).\0a\0aThe numeric codes are part of the wire format.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eRecoveryAction\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00`Lost-key recovery: replace designated credentials in an agreed\0asnapshot of the current document.\00\00\00\07LostKey\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00YCompromise recovery: restore the enrolled baseline, with designated\0acredentials replaced.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aCompromise\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\1eCancel one identified attempt.\00\00\00\00\00\06Cancel\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\83Change or remove the enrolled recovery configuration (the evidence a\0a`Protected` account needs in addition to owner authorization).\00\00\00\00\0bReconfigure\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00tApprove one scheduled account upgrade (the evidence a `Protected`\0aaccount needs in addition to owner authorization).\00\00\00\07Upgrade\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\04\00\00\008Everything encoding a statement or its parts can refuse.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eStatementError\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00-`account` is not a contract (`C...`) address.\00\00\00\00\00\00\12AccountNotContract\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\000`controller` is not a contract (`C...`) address.\00\00\00\15ControllerNotContract\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00wA credential names an address shape the recovery stack does not accept (muxed, claimable-balance, liquidity-pool, ...).\00\00\00\00\12UnsupportedAddress\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00zA replacement set's signer ids are not strictly ascending (sorted, no duplicates), so it has no single canonical encoding.\00\00\00\00\00\18ReplacementsNotCanonical\00\00\00\04\00\00\00#A replacement set replaces nothing.\00\00\00\00\11EmptyReplacements\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00@The current ledger is past the statement's `valid_until_ledger`.\00\00\00\0fEvidenceExpired\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00yA provider-chosen `valid_until_ledger` reaches further past the current ledger than the enrolled `expiry_ledgers` allows.\00\00\00\00\00\00\15EvidenceWindowTooLong\00\00\00\00\00\00\07\00\00\00\01\00\00\00&The subject of an `Upgrade` statement.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eUpgradeSubject\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00;The account's per-account, never-reused upgrade request id.\00\00\00\00\0arequest_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00<The exact Wasm hash the account would run after the upgrade.\00\00\00\09wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\01\00\00\00+Timing terms, all in ledger-sequence units.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fStatementTiming\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00fThe enrolled `delay-ledgers`: ledgers between an attempt becoming\0aauthorized and becoming completable.\00\00\00\00\00\0ddelay_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\d0The enrolled `expiry-ledgers`: the evidence window for a collecting\0aattempt, the completion window for an authorized one, and the upper\0abound on how far ahead a provider-chosen `valid_until_ledger` may\0areach.\00\00\00\0eexpiry_ledgers\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\01\aaThe last ledger sequence (inclusive) at which this evidence may be\0aaccepted. The controller fixes it for attempt-bound actions:\0a`LostKey`/`Compromise` use the attempt's evidence deadline, and\0a`Cancel` the last ledger the attempt could possibly be live, so\0aapprovals collected over several transactions all sign one\0astatement. For `Reconfigure`/`Upgrade` the evidence provider chooses\0ait, within `expiry_ledgers` of submission.\00\00\00\00\00\12valid_until_ledger\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\9dThe action-specific part of a statement. The variant determines\0a[`RecoveryStatement::action`]; there is no separate action field that\0acould disagree with it.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10StatementSubject\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\01\00\00\00*A lost-key attempt's initiation statement.\00\00\00\00\00\07LostKey\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eAttemptSubject\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00,A compromise attempt's initiation statement.\00\00\00\0aCompromise\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eAttemptSubject\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13Cancel one attempt.\00\00\00\00\06Cancel\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0dCancelSubject\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00,Change or remove the enrolled configuration.\00\00\00\0bReconfigure\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cConfigChange\00\00\00\01\00\00\00BApprove one account upgrade request, checked when it is scheduled.\00\00\00\00\00\07Upgrade\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eUpgradeSubject\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\000The one recovery statement. See the module docs.\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11RecoveryStatement\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\003The recovering account. Must be a contract address.\00\00\00\00\07account\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\009The enrolled configuration and epoch the evidence is for.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06config\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0dConfigBinding\00\00\00\00\00\00\a0The controller instance evaluating the evidence (for `Reconfigure`,\0athe currently adopted one, even when the change adopts another).\0aMust be a contract address.\00\00\00\0acontroller\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00`The network id (`sha256` of the network passphrase), as\0a`Env::ledger().network_id()` returns it.\00\00\00\0anetwork_id\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\1bWhat the evidence approves.\00\00\00\00\07subject\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\10StatementSubject\00\00\00=The enrolled timing terms and the evidence's freshness bound.\00\00\00\00\00\00\06timing\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fStatementTiming\00")
